.TH rstop 1  "rstop 0.1.8"
.SH NAME
rstop \- One terminal. Your whole system. CPU, GPU, containers and services.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrstop\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-view\fR] [\fB\-\-gpu\-panel\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gpu\fR] [\fB\-\-samples\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-process\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-read\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-full\-sampling\fR] [\fB\-\-layout\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-free\-mib\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-total\-mib\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-gpu\-utilization\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-memory\-utilization\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-config\-exec\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
One terminal. Your whole system. CPU, GPU, containers and services.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR
Sampling interval in milliseconds (250..=10000)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR
Color theme (also adjustable in F2 settings)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
midnight
.IP \(bu 2
nord
.IP \(bu 2
ember
.IP \(bu 2
black
.IP \(bu 2
white
.IP \(bu 2
graphite
.IP \(bu 2
ocean
.IP \(bu 2
forest
.IP \(bu 2
sand
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI<VIEW>\fR

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
overview
.IP \(bu 2
processes
.IP \(bu 2
gpu
.IP \(bu 2
storage
.IP \(bu 2
network
.IP \(bu 2
system
.IP \(bu 2
containers
.IP \(bu 2
services
.IP \(bu 2
explorer
.IP \(bu 2
history
.IP \(bu 2
events
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\-panel\fR \fI<GPU_PANEL>\fR [default: summary]
Initial GPU display; device opens Device info (history aliases summary)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
summary
.IP \(bu 2
history
.IP \(bu 2
device
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Alternate configuration file
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gpu\fR
Disable GPU driver queries
.TP
\fB\-\-samples\fR \fI<SAMPLES>\fR
Number of samples; emits newline\-delimited JSON, or fills SVG graph history
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR [default: 160]

.TP
\fB\-\-height\fR \fI<HEIGHT>\fR [default: 48]

.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-process\-network\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-read\-only\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-full\-sampling\fR
Preload all pages and keep their background sampling active
.TP
\fB\-\-layout\fR \fI<LAYOUT>\fR

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
balanced
.IP \(bu 2
compute
.IP \(bu 2
storage
.IP \(bu 2
minimal
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-free\-mib\fR \fI<MIN_FREE_MIB>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-min\-total\-mib\fR \fI<MIN_TOTAL_MIB>\fR [default: 0]
Minimum total VRAM for GPU selection
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-gpu\-utilization\fR \fI<MAX_GPU_UTILIZATION>\fR
GPU selection ceiling; devices with unknown utilization are excluded
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-memory\-utilization\fR \fI<MAX_MEMORY_UTILIZATION>\fR
GPU selection memory\-controller utilization ceiling
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-config\-exec\fR
Disable configured probes and alert commands
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rstop\-monitor(1)
Open the interactive system monitor (also the default command)
.TP
rstop\-snapshot(1)
Print one JSON snapshot, including process command lines
.TP
rstop\-sample(1)
Print newline\-delimited JSON samples (ten by default)
.TP
rstop\-record(1)
Record telemetry while monitoring; \-\-samples selects headless recording
.TP
rstop\-replay(1)
Replay a local recording; \-\-samples selects JSON output
.TP
rstop\-export(1)
Export live telemetry or a recording to CSV or SVG
.TP
rstop\-gpu(1)
Open the GPU view or select CUDA devices
.TP
rstop\-network(1)
Open connection monitoring, test a target, or capture packets
.TP
rstop\-doctor(1)
Explain resource problems, recent trends and useful next steps
.TP
rstop\-config(1)
Print the configuration path or write current preferences
.TP
rstop\-completions(1)
Generate shell completions without reading configuration
.TP
rstop\-man(1)
Print the manual page without reading configuration
.TP
rstop\-update(1)
Update this installer\-managed copy of rstop
.TP
rstop\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Monitor another host over SSH: rstop [OPTIONS] [user@]host[:port] [gpu|network]
Also accepts ssh://[user@]host[:port] and ~/.ssh/config aliases.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.8
